Electrical Measurement Analyzer

A small Python-based electrical measurement analyzer that calculates basic circuit quantities and classifies measurements against predefined limits.

Features
Calculates electrical power from voltage and current
Calculates resistance using voltage and current
Checks whether calculated power exceeds a specified limit
Classifies voltage as LOW, NORMAL, or HIGH
Handles invalid numerical input
Handles division-by-zero errors
Repeats measurements using a while loop
Separates reusable electrical calculations into a Python module

main.py

Contains the main program logic, including:

User input
Error handling
Measurement loop
Displaying results
electricals.py

Contains reusable functions for:

Power calculation
Resistance calculation
Power-limit checking
Voltage classification
Calculations

Power:

P = V × I

Resistance:

R = V / I
Default Limits
Parameter	Limit
Power	100 W
Normal voltage range	10–50 V
Example
Enter voltage: 24
Enter current: 3

=== Electrical Measurement ===
Voltage: 24.0 V
Current: 3.0 A
Resistance: 8.00 ohms
Power: 72.00 W
Power Status: NORMAL
Voltage Status: NORMAL
